{"id":"G2018","lemma":"ἐπιφέρω","transliteration":"epipherō","sayIt":"epipherō","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"verb","gloss":"to inflict","meaning":"ἐπι-φέρω\n[in LXX chiefly for שָׁלַח ;]\n1. to bring upon or against: κρίσιν, Ju 9.\n2. to impose, inflict: Rom.3:5.†\n(AS)","glosses":["inflict","bring"],"count":2,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"rom-3","v":5,"renderings":{"bsb":"to inflict","kjv":"who taketh"}},{"chapterId":"jud-1","v":9,"renderings":{"bsb":"to bring","kjv":"bring against him"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"Romans 3:5","note":"But if our unrighteousness commends the righteousness of God, what will we say? Is God unrighteous who inflicts wrath? I speak like men do.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Jude 1:9","note":"But Michael, the archangel, when contending with the devil and arguing about the body of Moses, dared not bring against him an abusive condemnation, but said…","source":"web"}],"related":[{"id":"G20180","lemma":"βασκανία","transliteration":"baskania","gloss":"jealousy"},{"id":"G20181","lemma":"βιβλιοφυλάκιον","transliteration":"bibliophulakion","gloss":"archives"},{"id":"G20182","lemma":"βλαστάω","transliteration":"blastaō","gloss":"to bring forth"},{"id":"G20183","lemma":"βόμβησις","transliteration":"bombēsis","gloss":"buzzing"},{"id":"G20184","lemma":"βοοζύγιον","transliteration":"boozugion","gloss":"ox-yoke"},{"id":"G20185","lemma":"βραχυτελής","transliteration":"brachutelēs","gloss":"brief"},{"id":"G20186","lemma":"βρῶμος","transliteration":"brōmos","gloss":"stink"},{"id":"G20187","lemma":"βύβλινος","transliteration":"bublinos","gloss":"papyrus"}],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}